{
  "id": "Compound::DB01087 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Primaquine exerts its effects through a series of mechanistic steps that ultimately lead to the inhibition of Cyp3a4. The evidence suggests that Primaquine binds to Cyp2d6, which is involved in the metabolism of xenobiotics and aromatase activity. This binding may modulate the activity of Cyp2d6, which in turn influences the metabolism of substrates that are subsequently processed by Cyp3a4. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Primaquine to Cyp3a4, including those involving oxidoreductase activity, underscores the complexity of the metabolic interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Primaquine to influence the expression or activity of Cyp3a4 through its interaction with Cyp2d6, thereby affecting the metabolism of various compounds. The consistent scores across the different paths suggest a robust and well-supported mechanism, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the precise role of Cyp2d6 in this process.",
